{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'driver|cadence|single|concurr|mirror-cursor' docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md src/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc; sed -n '350,410p' src/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc; rg -n 'cursor|reading' src/cljc/dao/stream/ringbuffer.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:290:goes): the caller's own polling is the cadence, and no driver step exists.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:410:Channel compositions are stepped and driver-paced: cadence is owned by the\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:415:  enforces an upper bound on active concurrent sessions. When `:max-sessions`\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:420:  in milliseconds, measured against the driver-supplied `now`; its alias\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:428:  floods from starving other processing or hanging driver ticks. An\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:463:composition drives at its own cadence, as it drives `endpoint-step`.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:579:pairs in its table, and the fanout of one driver step. A meeting request M\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:584:cadence is bounded by the NAT binding's lifetime, tens of seconds for UDP,\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:599:**The toy.** Peer B holds a handle `s` over the single value `\"hello\"`,\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:657:  can exist, and keep-alive cadence is the peer's own (section 4).\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc:29:   Every step here is driver-paced: the composition owns the cadence,\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc:94:  \"Drive the projection once, at the composition's cadence: read the\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc:199:   integer or nil, bounds concurrent active sessions. `:idle-timeout`,\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc:302:   the driver alone steps the acceptor.\"\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc:477:        mirror-cursor (atom (:dao.stream/cursor\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc:484:           :mirror-cursor mirror-cursor :policy policy\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc:575:   cadence: the attachment's projection first, so what the wire\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc:582:  (let [{:keys [ring table names channel mirror-cursor step-budget]\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc:588:      ;; driver alone steps the dial, as accept-step! does.\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc:589:      (reset! mirror-cursor\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc:590:              (remote/mirror-step table names ring @mirror-cursor handle\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc:592:    @mirror-cursor))\n                      :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor\n                                (stream/cursor (:ring media)\n                                               stream/anchor-oldest))\n                      :project (projection\n                                 {:attachment attachment\n                                  :traffic (:reader media)\n                                  :cursor (:cursor media)\n                                  :ring (:ring media)})\n                      :last-activity-ms (or now 0)})\n              (stream/close! handle))))))))\n\n\n(defn accept-step!\n  \"Advance the accepting composition one tick at `now`, in the order\n   serving compositions use: a transport step first (releasing dead\n   pendings, consuming standing acknowledgements), then one offer per\n   slot adopted with its fresh media and acknowledgement, then a second\n   transport step, so the fresh acknowledgement is consumed and the\n   accept frame is on the wire before this end answers anything,\n   then per session the projection and, over the projected reader and\n   the socket handle, the mirror step. Each session step is isolated in\n   a try/catch so an unexpected error marks the session closed and frees\n   its resources without bringing down the acceptor loop or healthy\n   peers. A session whose projection has closed or which has timed out\n   is then removed: repeated connections must not accumulate. Returns\n   the acceptor.\"\n  [acceptor now]\n  (let [{:keys [endpoint slots] :as s} @acceptor]\n    (ws/endpoint-step endpoint now)\n    (doseq [[index slot] (map-indexed vector slots)]\n      (let [r (stream/next (:offer-reader slot)\n                           (nth (:offer-cursors s) index))]\n        (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n          (swap! acceptor assoc-in [:offer-cursors index]\n                 (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n          (adopt! acceptor slot (:dao.stream/value r) now))))\n    (ws/endpoint-step endpoint now)\n    (doseq [[attachment session] (:sessions @acceptor)]\n      (try\n        (let [read-from (reading-cursor (:project session))\n              _ (step! (:project session) (:step-budget @acceptor))\n              cursor (remote/mirror-step (:table @acceptor)\n                                         (:names @acceptor)\n                                         (:ring session)\n                                         (:cursor session)\n                                         (:handle session)\n                                         (mirror-bounds @acceptor))\n              active? (or (not= read-from (reading-cursor (:project session)))\n                          (not= (:cursor session) cursor))]\n          (swap! acceptor update-in [:sessions attachment]\n                 #(cond-> (assoc % :cursor cursor)\n                    (and active? (some? now)) (assoc :last-activity-ms now))))\n        (catch #?(:clj Throwable :cljs :default :cljd Object) _\n          ;; Isolate the failure: close this session, spare the rest.\n          (close-session-resources! session)\n          (swap! acceptor assoc-in [:sessions attachment :closed?] true))))\n    (reap-sessions! acceptor now)\n    acceptor))\n\n\n(defn sessions\n25:  ;; The logical identity is carried in descriptors and cursors.  It therefore\n55:  (cursor\n62:                                    :dao.stream/cursor\n66:                                    :dao.stream/cursor\n73:    [_ cursor-value]\n76:        (not (map? cursor-value)) (result :dao.stream/invalid-cursor)\n77:        (not (contains? cursor-value :dao.stream.ringbuffer/identity))\n78:        (result :dao.stream/invalid-cursor)\n79:        (not= (:identity s) (:dao.stream.ringbuffer/identity cursor-value))\n80:        (result :dao.stream/cursor-mismatch)\n81:        (not (integer? (:dao.stream.ringbuffer/position cursor-value)))\n82:        (result :dao.stream/invalid-cursor)\n84:        (let [pos (:dao.stream.ringbuffer/position cursor-value)\n90:                   :dao.stream/cursor\n104:             :dao.stream/cursor {:dao.stream.ringbuffer/identity (:identity s)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
